{
    "background_story": "Aspen was a majestic wild mustang who roamed the open plains with her herd. Every year, as the seasons changed, they would make their great decampment to the greener pastures of the north. Aspen loved the thrill of the journey, feeling the wind in her mane and the sun on her back as she galloped alongside her companions. But one year, a severe drought hit the land, and the usual grazing grounds were barren and dry. Aspen's herd leader, a wise old mare named Oak, decided to lead the herd to a new, uncharted territory in search of better grazing. Aspen was hesitant at first, but her trust in Oak and the herd's unity kept her moving forward. Together, they braved the unknown, and Aspen discovered a new sense of resilience and adaptability within herself.",
